From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xob0t <32616886+xob0t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:09:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] Gaps reported with a marker: an address computation is
 marked, a note goes with its markers

Two ways a method could start with a Note but have no Opaque/Effect anywhere:

- An address computation into something no field was found in (an interior pointer
  of an object, say) was reported and then left as plain arithmetic on the reference:
  "conv.i8; ldc.i8 32; add", which is no valid IL and hides the gap. It is now the
  operand of an __address marker.
- A problem reported for a value whose marker is later dropped with the code that had
  it (a copy into a merged value nothing reads, a leftover register a call turned out
  not to take) stayed in the note, though the finished method has no gap there. The
  value markers now carry the problem they were made with (HOpaque.Problem); when none
  of a problem's markers is left in the finished method, the problem goes too
  (FlagMarkers; REWIND_NO_SITE_PROBLEMS turns this off). Problems without a marker of
  their own (exception handling, lifting) are never dropped.

Unity 6000.0 Master x64 game: 13 bodies with a note and no marker before, 0 after (5
now marked at the site, 8 no longer noted; their IL is otherwise unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
